 r←MarkUnavailablePackages r;bool;ids;found;RI;registries;request;res;ns;i;registry
⍝ Takes the matrix `CheckForLaterVersion` has built and marks every row whose installed version is
⍝ not hosted by any Registry with a priority greater than 0 any more, by saying so in [;2].\\
⍝ Only rows that offer no later version are looked at: where there is one, the version ahead is what
⍝ matters, not the one behind. Rows that already carry a "<<< ... >>>" marker are left alone.\\
⍝ A package that is not hosted anywhere cannot be installed again by anybody, including its author,
⍝ so the build list it sits in cannot be reproduced. Finding that out when the build list is checked
⍝ is a great deal better than finding it out when somebody tries to install it.\\
⍝ Must be called while the connections established by `CheckForLaterVersion` are still open.\\
⍝ A Registry that fails to answer contributes nothing and is passed over in silence: this is an
⍝ additional piece of information, and not being able to get it must not make the report fail.
 bool←(0=r[;4])∧'<'≠⊃¨r[;2]
 :If 0<+/bool
     ids←bool/r[;1]
     found←(≢ids)⍴0
     RI←RegistryIndices
     registries←1 ListRegistries''
     :If 0<≢registries←(registries[;RI.priority]>0)⌿registries
         request←R.NewRequest 0
         request.Headers,←⊂'Accept' 'application/json'
         :For i :In ⍳≢registries
             :If ∧/found
                 :Leave
             :EndIf
             registry←⊃registries[i;RI.url]
             :If Reg.IsHTTP registry
                 request.RequestTarget←Reg.VersionOf_REST,'/packages/exist/',1↓∊',',¨(~found)/ids
                 :Trap 0
                     res←SendAndReceive registry request
                     :If 200=res.StatusCode
                         ns←Reg.JSON res.Content
                         found[⍸(~found)\ns.exist]←1
                     :EndIf
                 :EndTrap
             :Else
                 found[⍸(~found)\F.IsDir registry∘,¨(~found)/ids]←1
             :EndIf
         :EndFor
         :If 0<+/~found
             r[⍸bool\~found;2]←⊂'<<< Not available any more >>>'
         :EndIf
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
⍝Done
